Spec: Application package

Purpose:
  The `aikana` Python package. It is organized into feature packages that follow the layering described in
  ./architecture.sdd, and it provides the entry point that composes and serves them as a FastHTML app.

Structure:
  ./__init__.py: package marker
  ./main.py: the composition root; builds the shared database connection and each feature's repository and
    service, registers every feature's routes on the FastHTML app, and binds to the `$PORT` environment variable
  ./architecture.sdd: the Ports and Adapters (Hexagonal) contract shared by every feature package below
  ./shared/: cross-cutting kernel (database connection, page layout shell) with no business rules of its own
  ./auth/: admin login, logout and the write guard used by other feature packages
  ./courses/: the Course entity
  ./semester/: the Semester entity and the semester wall planner view
  ./realizations/: the CourseRealization entity linking a Course, a Semester and a group to its Lessons, and the
    per-CourseRealization weekly calendar view
  ./lessons/: the Lesson entity
  ./holidays/: the Holiday entity
  ./day_dialog/: the admin dialog for adding or editing a Lesson or a Holiday on a given day

References:
  ./architecture.sdd

Owns:
  ./__init__.py
  ./main.py

Must:
  `python -m aikana.main` starts the server on the port given by `$PORT`, defaulting to `8000`.
  `main.py` registers the compiled Tailwind stylesheet as a static route (`app.static_route`) at `/static/app.css`,
  using `./shared/layout.py`'s `STATIC_DIR`, per ./shared/shared.sdd.
  Every feature package below has a same-basename spec inside it, following ./architecture.sdd.
  Views render for unauthenticated visitors without any editing affordances.

Tasks:
  [ ] Implement ./shared/, then ./auth/, then ./courses/ and ./semester/ (entities), then ./holidays/, then
    ./realizations/ and ./lessons/, then ./day_dialog/, and finally wire them together in ./main.py
  [x] Build a hardcoded first visual pass instead: ./shared/layout.py, ./courses/domain.py and a placeholder
    ./courses/services.py, ./semester/ (domain, placeholder services, view, routes), ./realizations/domain.py and a
    placeholder ./realizations/services.py, ./lessons/domain.py and a placeholder ./lessons/services.py, and
    ./holidays/domain.py and a placeholder ./holidays/services.py, then register ./semester/routes.py in ./main.py.
    ./auth/, ./day_dialog/, every ports.py/repository_sqlite.py and ./shared/db.py remain unimplemented until the
    persistence phase, so ./main.py does not yet construct repositories per ../architecture.sdd
  [x] Add the top-bar navigation and default-by-date Semester selection in ./shared/layout.py and ./semester/, and
    the per-CourseRealization weekly view with its own dropdown in ./realizations/view.py and ./realizations/routes.py,
    resolving ./courses/courses.sdd's former open per-view decision in favor of ./realizations/realizations.sdd;
    wire ./realizations/routes.py into ./main.py alongside ./semester/routes.py
